Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Faithfully\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 0, "end": 189, "text": "Faithfully (Faith Evans album) Faithfully is the third studio album by American singer Faith Evans, released by Bad Boy Records in the United States on November 6, 2001 (see 2001 in music)."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 190, "end": 328, "text": "Featuring production by Sean Combs, The Neptunes, Cory Rooney, Michael Angelo Saulsberry, Mario Winans, it peaked at number 14 on the U.S."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 329, "end": 380, "text": "\"Billboard\" 200 and was certified gold by the RIAA."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 381, "end": 494, "text": "The album spawned five total singles including Can't Believe featuring Carl Thomas, You Gets No Love featuring P."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 495, "end": 585, "text": "Diddy & Loon, the Billboard Top 40 hit, I Love You, and Alone in This World, respectfully."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d00", "start": 586, "end": 594, "text": "This was"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d01", "start": 0, "end": 52, "text": "contemporary R & B , funk music and hip hop genres ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d01", "start": 53, "end": 107, "text": "Quick Facts Studio album by Faith Evans , Released ..."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0434-56d078fd4aad:d01", "start": 108, "end": 556, "text": "Faithfully Studio album by Faith Evans Released November 6 , 2001 ( 2001-11-6 ) Length 61 : 19 Label Bad Boy Arista Producer Sean Combs Battlecat Bink Buckwild Hozay Clowney Kip Collins Faith Evans